! HCN -> HNC isomerization, HF/STO-3G transition state.
!
! Classic textbook system: H migrates around the rigid C-N axis.
! The TS is a bent geometry near R(CH) ~ R(NH) ~ 1.2 A, H about
! halfway between the two heavy atoms (a 3-membered "T" arrangement).
! At HF/STO-3G the barrier is ~50 kcal/mol from HCN; the precise
! number is not the point of this test -- the point is that:
!
!   * the optimizer converges in a reasonable number of steps
!     (typically 8-15) starting from a sensible TS guess geometry,
!   * the located stationary point has exactly ONE imaginary
!     frequency (the HCN <-> HNC mode, ~ 1300i cm^-1 at this level),
!   * energy at the TS is intermediate between HCN minimum and
!     HNC minimum.
!
! Job: ts+freq.  The Hessian is computed in-place at the input
! geometry (we did NOT supply %read_hess), so this exercises Path
! B of the JOB_OPT_TS dispatcher (auto-Hessian).  After convergence
! a freq pass at the located TS produces <stem>_ts.hess /
! <stem>_ts.molden (the second .hess pair, with the "_ts" label).
!
! Initial geometry: T-shape with H displaced perpendicularly from
! the C-N midpoint -- close to the known HF/STO-3G saddle, which
! sits at ~ 60-70 degree HCN/HNC opening.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     ts+freq
%charge  0
%mult    1
%hess_method  analytical
%ts_mode 1
%geom_maxiter 80
%geom angstrom
C   -0.55  -0.20   0.00
N    0.55  -0.20   0.00
H    0.00   0.95   0.00
*end
